    "bio": "A Representative from Tennessee; born in Fort Benning, Chattahoochee County, Ga., October 28, 1957; graduated from the McCallie School, Chattanooga, Tenn., 1976; attended University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill, N.C. and University of Tennessee; real estate broker; unsuccessful candidate for election to the One Hundred Third Congress in 1992; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Fourth and to the seven succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1995-January 3, 2011); not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Twelfth Congress in 2010, but was an unsuccessful candidate for nomination for Governor of Tennessee.",
